/-!
# ptmalloc versions, glibc 2.36: `__libc_malloc`'s bytes and its `tcache_get` sequence

The pin `debian_2_36_9_deb12u14` (glibc 2.36, Debian 12 `libc6` 2.36-9+deb12u14, gcc 12.2;
`Silmaril.Libc.Ptmalloc.Versions.pin236`): the 791 bytes of `__libc_malloc` at `0x98930`, transcribed from
the pinned file (`.text` file offsets equal virtual addresses; checked by
`scripts/ptmalloc/check-code.py`), and the fact that they carry gcc's
inlined `tcache_get` at offset 333 **with the bin in `rbp`**
(`X86sim.TcGetSeqR mallocCode 333 .rbp 4 4`: gcc 12 keeps the index in `rbp`, so
`lea 0x10(%rbp),%rdi` and `mov %cx,(%rdx,%rbp,2)` are 4 bytes each and the block 45 bytes; finding
V1-F3). With it the generic `X86sim.tcGetRun`/`tcGetCore`/`tcGetSim` hold for 2.36 with no new
proof (`tcGetRun236`).

2.36's `_int_free` inlines `tcache_put` in another instruction order (`tcache_key` loaded before
the bin test, the count in `esi`, `rax`/`rcx` as tcache/bin), so `X86sim.TcPutSeq` does not cover
it: its put block needs its own sequence bundle (open).
-/

@[expose] public section

